<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Martha's Vineyard</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Noepe</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Martha's Vineyard is an island off the south coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-cod">Cape Cod</a> in Massachusetts, the Wampanoag land of Noepe. English settlers under Thomas Mayhew arrived in the 1640s, and many of the island's Wampanoag became Christian converts. Governed under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> from 1671, it was joined to the Province of Massachusetts Bay by the charter of 1691.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marthas-vineyard.jpg" alt="Martha's Vineyard" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alex Wilcox Cheek · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marthasvineyard-Aquinnah-cliffs-summer.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
